Fail closed when a UML userspace stub cannot be cloned

A failed host clone in start_userspace is a host capacity failure, not a
guest fork failure. Returning -errno lets the guest observe it as ENOMEM,
possibly emit different events, and shut down normally under the same
profile and host identity. Exit the UML host process with a reserved status
after writing a diagnostic directly to stderr. The launcher classifies that
status as an infrastructure failure independently of console collection.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a kernel diff under
consonance/harmony-linux/linux/patches/ per the repository's kernel-patch
exception.

---
--- a/arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c
+++ b/arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c
@@ -438,6 +438,8 @@ __initcall(init_stub_exe_fd);
 
 int using_seccomp;
 
+#define HOST_CLONE_FAILED 87
+
 /**
  * start_userspace() - prepare a new userspace process
  * @mm_id: The corresponding struct mm_id
@@ -484,6 +486,8 @@ int start_userspace(struct mm_id *mm_id)
 		printk(UM_KERN_ERR "%s : clone failed, errno = %d\n",
 		       __func__, errno);
-		goto out_close;
+		write(STDERR_FILENO, "Harmony UML host clone failed\n",
+		      sizeof("Harmony UML host clone failed\n") - 1);
+		_exit(HOST_CLONE_FAILED);
 	}
 
 	if (using_seccomp) {
